# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the op-fusion programme's four-card window, WP5 (CCL options; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/fusion-1 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards
# are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head (sed -i 's/tp4-fusion-1/<tag>/' *.env). The fabric sweeps
# (P0-P4) run the probe from the checkout and need only an image with the models tree; the lever jobs need the image B0 built. The cards are under development.
# CCLS: the PLUMBING CONTROL audited: c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-ccl-served-audit (QWEN_FAST_CCL_OPTIONS=served plus the audit) over warmup and
# concurrent8_steady. The unit-major reduce-scatter hook and the DistributedNorm gather shim are engaged with an EMPTY set, so every call carries the values the model
# passes today and the audit compares each audited call with itself. READ: the engaged line (rs=128 or more, ag=128 or 129 a forward, fallbacks=0), the audit lines for both
# ops from a replay (round>=1, chips=4, exact=True) for each block, hashes equal to the production profile's. A fall-back line here is the census not matching the stack's
# own calls (the reason is in the line): fix the census before any set is read. Duration (estimate): 40 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-ccl-served-audit
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,concurrent8_steady
